.\\\\nReleased under the Apache License, Version 2.0, subject to upstream notices.\\\\n\\\\nAttribution and dependencies\\\\n\\\\nGoogle Quantum AI competition authors: task specifications, reference circuits,\\\\nKickmix simulator and unchanged official verification/file-reader code.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation\\\\n\\\\nRudra Bhaskar: direct polynomial phasing, retained coefficient table and\\\\nlow-memory arithmetic adapted by the inverse-square-root implementation.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/rudrabhaskar/direct-polynomial-phasing-verified-search?scriptVersionId=361364488\\\\n\\\\nLightningV08: compressed normalization flags.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/lightningv08/quantum-circuits-memory-algebra\\\\n\\\\nSumit Chongder: open centered signed-digit inverse-square-root generator,\\\\ncoefficient fitting, integer pipeline and arithmetic, retained and credited.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/sumitchongder/notebook2f196e646b?scriptVersionId=361357149\\\\nAdded adaptation: split high-word phasing, allocation after normalization,\\\\nfolded final carry, and borrowing a proven constant input bit as clean carry.\\\\nThe later 92-qubit revision reduces curvature precision F2 from 10 to 9,\\\\nregenerates the coefficient table, and certifies the complete promised input\\\\ndomain. Its same-table ordinary-schedule comparison has 102 qubits; the\\\\noriginal Sumit coefficient table and 103-qubit circuit remain credited above.\\\\n\\\\nKozykappa: physical ensemble compression, sparse column rotations, and prior\\\\npublic work on reachable-control simplification and clean-wire allocation.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kozykappa/quantum-circuits-sparse-sos-factors-and-circuit\\\\n\\\\nKozykorpesh / Kozykappa: two-address banked XOR QROM construction, adapted\\\\nfrom Sumit's public arithmetic and used for the chemistry angle lookup.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kozykappa/quantum-ai-compact-arithmetic-banked-qrom?scriptVersionId=361433617\\\\nKirill Tymchishin v10: integration of our public arithmetic/decoder/factors\\\\nwith that banked lookup, which supplies the comparison baseline for this release.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kirilltym/quantum-circuits-qrom-tower42?scriptVersionId=361453242\\\\nAdded adaptation: omit zero difference-bank columns and apply an exact\\\\nreversible CNOT change of output basis for dependent columns. Both tables\\\\nare transformed, preserving the XOR oracle on arbitrary input targets.\\\\n\\\\nk256.dev: public compiled DQI decoder and starting chemistry factorization.\\\\nThe decoder's original generator is not included in that publication.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/k256net/claude?scriptVersionId=361337610\\\\n\\\\nAccessible public dependency mirror: Kirill Tymchishin, version 7, labelled\\\\nApache 2.0 by Kaggle. Both reused artifacts are pinned by SHA-256. This mirror\\\\nlabel alone does not establish the full upstream ownership chain.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kirilltym/quantum-circuits-qrom-tower42?scriptVersionId=361358116\\\\n\\\\nAdded changes: split-phase scheduling and separate stage caches for invsqrt;\\\\nindependent bounded Boolean-polynomial circuit simplification for DQI;\\\\nalternating sparse rotations and effective-norm optimization for chemistry;\\\\nlayout/precision experiments, resource explanations and full verification reports.\\\\n\\\\nThe scored archive, generated candidates and public dependencies are identified\\\\nseparately in the notebook's reports. No endorsement by upstream authors is implied.\\\\n\\\\nCalibrated arithmetic revision\\\\n\\\\nKozykorpesh: published explicit calibrated integer coefficients and open\\\\nexact-domain minimax regeneration, plus transitive AND implications.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kozykappa/quantum-ai-compact-arithmetic-banked-qrom?scriptVersionId=361456406\\\\n\\\\nAlex Chilton: shared prefix normalization and empty-target temporary-AND\\\\nshift moves with measurement-based inverse and phase correction.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/alexchilton/where-the-toffolis-go-anatomy-a-cheaper-invsqrt?scriptVersionId=361472684\\\\n\\\\nOur additions in this revision: use the promised input bound to replace\\\\nmutually exclusive inverted-top-bit ANDs by affine logic; algebraic-normal-\\\\nform lookup and measurement-phase cleanup for the exact chemistry words;\\\\na fast C++ binary implementation of Kozykorpesh's implication pass with\\\\nvalidated globally-clean conditional facts. The resulting DQI binary is\\\\nidentical to Kozykorpesh's published output, not a new decoder design.\\\\nThe original generator/compiled-input limits and notices above still apply.\\\\n\\\\nFinal derivative-split integration\\\\n\\\\nRudra Bhaskar: derivative residual/coarse representation, top-carry reuse,\\\\nand static-high phase checkpoint generator, published under Apache-2.0.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/rudrabhaskar/highest-public-score-direct-polynomial-phasing?scriptVersionId=361445283\\\\nKirill Tymchishin v11: integration of that generator with Alex Chilton's\\\\nnormalization and empty-target shift schedules; the 95-qubit baseline.\\\\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/code/kirilltym/quantum-circuits-qrom-tower42?scriptVersionId=361491814\\\\nOur final integration generalizes the derivative-split widths for the\\\\nexplicit Kozykorpesh table, borrows one normalized constant input bit as\\\\nan adder carry, and applies the promised-input top-bit affine identity.\\\\nThe three ablation rows retain the same coefficient model.\\\\n\\\", encoding='utf-8')\\nprint('LICENSE and NOTICE written beside the reports and submission archive.')\\n\"},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"82c75cb3\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":\"## Sources, attribution and limits\\n\\n- [Sumit Chongder, open signed-digit generator](https://www.kaggle.com/code/sumitchongder/notebook2f196e646b?scriptVersionId=361357149): centered signed digits, coefficient fitting, fixed-point pipeline, normalization and arithmetic. Apache-2.0 as published.\\n- [Kozykorpesh, calibrated arithmetic and banked QROM, v2](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kozykappa/quantum-ai-compact-arithmetic-banked-qrom?scriptVersionId=361456406): the explicit calibrated coefficient table and exact-domain regeneration algorithm, the banked XOR lookup adapted from Sumit, and the transitive AND-implication pass. The fast DQI output in this notebook is **byte-identical to that publication**. We add direct binary compilation, tested global branch facts and the chemistry polynomial schedule; we do not claim the published 231-gate improvement as our discovery.\\n- [Alex Chilton, arithmetic anatomy, v3](https://www.kaggle.com/code/alexchilton/where-the-toffolis-go-anatomy-a-cheaper-invsqrt?scriptVersionId=361472684): shared prefix normalization and temporary-AND shifts into empty targets. We combine these with the derivative-split generator and Kozykorpesh's precision, then add our carry borrowing and promised-input simplification. The fixed-table ablation isolates our two additions. This exact public version has observed score **5.69358** as checked on 23 October 2026.\\n- [Rudra Bhaskar, derivative splitting and static-high phasing, v7](https://www.kaggle.com/code/rudrabhaskar/highest-public-score-direct-polynomial-phasing?scriptVersionId=361445283): the derivative residual/coarse representation, top-carry reuse and high-phase checkpoint generator. Apache-2.0 is confirmed by the exact public page. We generalize the compiler widths to use the calibrated table and add carry borrowing and input-domain logic.\\n- [Kirill Tymchishin, QROM + Tower42, v11](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kirilltym/quantum-circuits-qrom-tower42?scriptVersionId=361491814): integrates the Rudra and Alex schedules; its 95-qubit arithmetic cost **168,521.1256** supplies a historical comparison. Its published combined **5.724688 is a projection**, with no newer observed score confirmed at this snapshot. Version 10 integrated the banked lookup with our factors.\\n- [Our scored 5.67004 archive](https://www.kaggle.com/code/anazemcev/vqcc-banked-clean-staging): baseline submission 57562270. [Signed-Digit Memory v1](https://www.kaggle.com/code/anazemcev/quantum-circuits-signed-digit-memory?scriptVersionId=361422248) and [Open QROM v4](https://www.kaggle.com/code/anazemcev/quantum-circuits-open-qrom-measured-gains?scriptVersionId=361406534) document the earlier split-phase memory schedule, bounded Boolean-polynomial DQI pass and effective-norm optimization. The baseline DQI and factor NPZ enter this run with SHA-256 guards; the DQI and every quantum circuit are then replaced or rebuilt.\\n\\nThe underlying decoder binary and starting chemistry factors originate with [k256.dev's public compilation](https://www.kaggle.com/code/k256net/claude?scriptVersionId=361337610), accessible through [Kirill's Apache-labelled v7 mirror](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kirilltym/quantum-circuits-qrom-tower42?scriptVersionId=361358116). [Kozykorpesh's earlier chemistry work](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kozykappa/quantum-circuits-sparse-sos-factors-and-circuit) supplied physical compression and sparse rotations. The decoder generator was not supplied. The mirror's license label does not establish the complete upstream ownership chain; the inherited binary dependency remains explicit.\\n\\n[Official evaluation](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation/overview/evaluation), [metric](https://www.kaggle.com/code/metric/google-quantum-ai-metric), distributed verifier source and [competition rules](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation/rules) define the contract. Thresholds, confidence bounds and reference data are unchanged. Implementation and explanations were prepared with AI assistance. Full sampled verification is circuit evidence; the exact integer and table identities have separate certificates.\\n\\nThe output retains generators, reports, member hashes, LICENSE, NOTICE and the submission archive. The displayed combined verifier value is a development projection. **Submit to Competition** on the completed notebook version establishes its observed score, shown by Kaggle's badge.\\n\"}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\",\"version\":\"3.13\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}",
